{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l as the dominant architecture (0.706–0.725 vs. 0.518–0.542 for scgpt), and transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool by ~2 points (config_039: 0.725 vs. config_008: 0.706). The only untested dimension within this clearly best subspace is the fusion method: all scvi_n200 results so far use 'weighted' fusion. Config_031 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) directly tests whether concat fusion can push accuracy beyond the current best of 0.725. With scgpt, concat was slightly worse than weighted (0.518 vs. 0.542), but the interaction with the much stronger scvi_n200 representation may differ. This is the highest-value exploitation step: it refines the single most promising configuration. Expected cost is moderate-to-high (~5–7 GPU hours) because concat fusion increases parameter count (as seen in config_021 at 7.18 h vs. config_020 at 2.94 h), but the transformer aggregation component keeps it comparable to config_039's 3.60 h baseline; I estimate roughly 5–6 GPU hours. With 3 experiments remaining after this one, confirming or improving the top configuration is the best use of the next slot."
}

